  "notes": "A clean nine-bullet ladder that maps almost one-to-one onto steps, with one merge worth explaining. Bullet 5 is FOUR trades to the same goblin in the same spot -- one ash for the Dusty tome, two for the Pointed jug, three for the Cracked club, four for the Peeling hairpin -- so it is one step whose items are the ten ash those four trades cost between them, and whose evidence is all four key items held at once. Splitting it into four rungs on one NPC would be four markers on the same dot. Bullet 6 is likewise four conversations with Ravorara and stays one step.\n\nThe eleventh ash is a separate step because it is a different action with a different answer ('No Thanks') and a different key item, and because the page deliberately separates it. Hoary Bomb Ash x11 is evidence on step 4 only; steps 5 and 7 spend it, and the same item may not anchor two steps.\n\nGrid conflict: bullet 3 puts Brakobrik at (K-10) and bullets 5 and 7 put him at (K-11). Each is recorded where the page wrote it rather than reconciled, since the walk from one to the other is a few paces and nothing in the page says which is right. The page contradicting itself about one entity's position is what holds this quest at medium rather than high; the ladder itself is not in doubt.",
