  "notes": "Two bullets, two steps, and the only judgement here is what to do with bullet 1's fork. The Ordrynite comes either from Cryptonberry Plaguers and Stalkers inside Pso'Xja or from Chocobo Digging in Beaucedine Glacier -- two different zones for one step, and a step has one zone. Rather than pick a side and put a marker in the wrong half of the world, the step carries no zone at all and both routes live in the note; the two mobs are still recorded with role 'drop' so the digging branch costs nothing. The sub-sub-bullets under bullet 1 are travel shortcuts (Outpost Warp, Survival Guide, HP1 plus Escape) and Chocobo Digging rank advice, not steps.\n\nThe 'Name Options' section after the walkthrough is the reward itself -- a four-column table of airship name segments you pick from -- and contains no action. Its footnote (ten completions unlock the fourth segment) is a repeat count, not a step; the header already says Repeatable: Y.",
