  "notes": "The canonical unordered-group quest. Bullet 2 is a bare twenty-row table of area, position and name with no ordering language at all, and the game imposes none -- so all twenty share one group and draw at once. A strict ladder would mark Daggao and then nothing until you happened to walk past him. The twenty span four zones, and each step keeps the zone and grid the table gave it: one step, one zone, even inside a group.\n\nNo evidence anywhere in the group. The badge is granted whole at step 1 and taken back whole at step 22; nothing in the packets counts how many of the twenty you have spoken to, so the middle of this quest is genuinely untrackable and the runtime falls back on the session latch across it. The Red invitation card is NOT used as evidence on the last step -- the header lists it under Reward, so holding it proves the quest is over rather than that a step is done.\n\n'Quest Reqs: Access to Chateau d'Oraguille' is real (five of the twenty are inside it) but has no schema slot and no observable predicate, so it is flagged and gates nothing. Both bullets of the 'Notes' section are things you do AFTER joining Salaheem's Sentinels -- claiming Imperial currency from Naja Salaheem and paying Alib-Mufalib 300 gil for a teleport -- and neither belongs to this quest's ladder.",
