  ],
  "notes": "The Geomancer unlock, and it has two forks that are OR, not AND. Bullet 2's three crags are one per home nation and you can only use yours; bullet 4's three Ergon Loci are three places any of which will do. Both are modelled as groups, because a group draws all its members at once and that is exactly the right picture for a fork whose branch the addon cannot know -- nothing in the packets reports your home nation.\n\nFollowing the pattern the monuments quest established, the crag group's soil key item sits on the LAST member only. Duplicate evidence across steps is a hard gate, and putting it last means obtaining the soil lands the mark on Sylvie rather than back inside the group. The charging group carries no evidence at all: bullet 6's 'You feel a mystical warmth welling up inside you!' is a chat line, the Luopan key item is already in hand from step 5 and does not change when it warms, so up to eight minutes of resting is genuinely invisible.\n\nBullet 2 names the object 'the Ergon Locus ???', so it is recorded as the object Ergon Locus -- the page's own words -- while bullet 4's three are individually named and keep those names. Step 5 requires holding BOTH the Petrified Log item and the soil key item, which is why the key item appears in items as well. The trailing WARNING bullet is about not tossing the Matre Bell before a much later Empyrean quest; it is a caution about the reward, not a step.\n\nMoved out of the player-facing step notes (build vocabulary; see AUTHORING.md, 'Two notes, two audiences'):\n  step 8: Any one of the three will do; none of them is observable, so the group carries no evidence.",
