  "confidence": "high",
  "review_flags": [
   "unordered_group",
   "zone_unnamed"
  ],
  "notes": "Straightforward except for one thing the page never says. Bullet 2 sends you to 'the Scouts' Coalition' to talk to Wegellion at (F-9) and names no zone anywhere on the page -- and (F-9) falls inside both Adoulin halves, so it cannot be inferred from the grid either. Rather than guess, that step's zone is null. A zone-less row matches everywhere, so Wegellion still gets a marker; it is only less precise, which is the correct trade against naming the wrong zone.\n\nBullets 4 and 5 are one search: bullet 4 is Emjook-Renook telling you the three grids and bullet 5 is you checking them, so they merge into a group of three Suspicious Places. Only one of the three holds the badge and which one is random, so a strict ladder would be wrong two times in three; the group draws all three and the badge sits on the last member so that obtaining it moves the mark on to Emjook-Renook. The long sub-bullets under each are walking directions and bush-obstruction times, not steps.\n\nStep 1's grid is the header's (J-8); bullet 1 writes it '(J-7/J-8)' and the two are the same NPC. The 'hand over the hat' sub-bullet under bullet 2 is a dialogue branch on that same conversation, not a separate rung.",
