  "notes": "Five bullets, four of which are steps. Bullet 1 is a cooldown -- one game day must pass after Gifts of the Griffon before this will start -- and game time is not something the addon can see, so it is a gate that gates nothing and is recorded here rather than as a rung. Bullet 2 is two conversations with Rholont separated by a zone-out; both are the same marker on the same NPC, so they are one step with the round trip in the note.\n\nThe start is Rholont and agrees with the header; the zone entry is step 2, mid-quest, not the start. Bullet 3 is a real step even though there is nothing to click: the cutscene fires on entering Jugner Forest (S) and ONLY when you come in from East Ronfaure (S), so the route is load-bearing and any other way in silently fails. Bullets 4 and 5 are three actions on one ??? at (I-6) -- touch for a cutscene, touch again to pop the NM, kill it, touch a third time to finish -- which is three rungs, because the fight between them is a different kind of thing and the guide's own example splits exactly this shape.\n\nThe quest ends on the ??? with no hand-in NPC, so the last step is unmarkable by construction and no turn-in is invented. The Angelstone is the header's Reward and so is not evidence on it. The 'Notes' section is about activating a later Wings of the Goddess mission at the Cavernous Maws and the 'Lore' table is a spoiler box; neither is a step.",
